Unlike this repo's other third_party/ entries (whole vendored trees built
from CMake/source), this is a single-file NEAR-VERBATIM ADAPTATION, not a
vendor import — the file lives in the main source tree, not here, because
it is one integrated module of greenboost-cli, not a standalone dependency
this repo builds against. This NOTICE exists purely to satisfy the
attribution requirement for that adapted file; the file itself carries its
own Apache-2.0 SPDX header.

What was adapted
-----------------
`greenboost-cli/greenboost_cli/instruments/capture.py` — the stdlib-only
bounded/redacting-capture core (`_CaptureBudget`, `_bounded_string`,
`_scrub_secret_values`, `_redact_capture_key`, `_capture_jsonable`, plus the
standalone/anchored/truncated credential-pattern tuples and the aggregate-
budget constants) from:

  agents/langchain-deepagents-code/nemoclaw_observability.py

as it existed in the NemoClaw checkout audited on 2026-08-05 (commit
87fcfe40d, "docs(policy): add N1X platform taxonomy (#8232)").

Ported near-verbatim rather than re-derived because the secret-shaped-value
redaction is subtle security code (byte-boundary-safe truncation handling,
unpaired-UTF-16-surrogate replacement, credential-shaped dict-key detection
across snake_case/camelCase/PascalCase naming) — re-deriving it from
scratch risked silently missing an edge case the original already handles.
See the NemoClaw audit plan's Phase 3d for the full port rationale.

What was NOT carried over: NemoClaw's LangGraph checkpoint/interrupt-state
redaction (`_STATE_CAPTURE_KEYS`), its OTLP export lifecycle/exporter
classes, and `_bounded_llm_request` — none of that applies to GreenBoost's
use (bounding a tool call's `params` dict before a dataflux JSONL emit, not
exporting LLM request payloads over OTLP). Variable and constant names were
renamed where they referenced NemoClaw-specific concepts ("Relay" → "safe
JSON", OTLP terminology dropped) without changing the underlying logic.

